{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1283257-do-the-primordials-embody-their-concepts-or-do-they-just-represent-them","id":1283257,"title":"do the primordials embody their concepts or do they just represent them?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-01-28T07:39:54-08:00","id":1283257,"title":"do the primordials embody their concepts or do they just represent them?","content":"In other words if i kill SWLIHN do i weaken the very idea of order and hierarhcy? I believe that at least in second edition this was the overall implication but i'm not sure","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T07:59:36-08:00","id":1283262,"title":"","content":"I think this may have been true at some point, but by making creation they sort of off-loaded the concepts onto gods. <br /> <br /> Nowadays they're less the core pillar of a concept and more the prototype.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T08:13:39-08:00","id":1283265,"title":"","content":"Neither the Yozis nor the Gods embody anything but themselves.<br /> <br /> Exalted is fundamentally an existentialist game and setting in a very meaningful sense; existence precedes essence. The ideas projected onto things (like order and hierarchy) are just that- projections, not things-in-themselves.<br /> <br /> Now, the Yozis can get a little weird in this regard, cause they will be said to *create* things that, uh, can't be reasoned about as having been created in this framework- like creating sorrow so they could mourn, or the Ebon Dragon creating justice so he could cheat it. But chalk that up to mythology is weird; the things created, once created, are independent of the creators.<br /> <br /> Likewise, the Gods are just in charge of monitoring things; they make sure that grass grows, the sun shines, and birds sing- but without the gods, the grass would still exist (and probably still grow), the sun would still shine (but maybe the wrong color or too brightly or dim), and the birds would still fly and chirp- but their songs may get confused. You do not kill a river by killing the river god; you do not break the hierarchy loved by She Who Lives In Her Name by destroying her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T08:28:27-08:00","id":1283269,"title":"","content":"Actually I think in 3E one of the defining qualities of the Incarnae is supposed to be that they break this rule. The Unconquered Sun really is the sun, and if he died it may well go out. <br /> <br /> But yeah, most other gods aren't nearly as vital for the thing they represent. Kill a god, another will soon take it's place, and up in heaven there's gods of stuff in general to oversee everything. It's hard to say what would happen if they were <i>all</i> wiped out, but creation is pretty much self sustaining now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T08:35:40-08:00","id":1283272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1283257-do-the-primordials-embody-their-concepts-or-do-they-just-represent-them?p=1283269#post1283269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually I think in 3E one of the defining qualities of the Incarnae is supposed to be that they break this rule. The Unconquered Sun really is the sun, and if he died it may well go out.<br /> <br /> But yeah, most other gods aren't nearly as vital for the thing they represent. Kill a god, another will soon take it's place, and up in heaven there's gods of stuff in general to oversee everything. It's hard to say what would happen if they were <i>all</i> wiped out, but creation is pretty much self sustaining now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't... think that's the case? I just did a scan of the corebook regarding the Incarnae, and nothing suggesting that jumps out at me.<br /> <br /> Was this word of dev that I missed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T08:39:01-08:00","id":1283274,"title":"","content":"A combination of &quot;The Sun is The Sun&quot; and the fact that that's kinda what Incarnate means.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T08:40:23-08:00","id":1283276,"title":"","content":"Killing She Who Lives in Her Name would not destroy the concept of hierarchy.<br /> <br /> Moreover, the Yozis aren't simply manifest concepts. They aren't Nobilis-style Imperators.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T13:12:45-08:00","id":1283336,"title":"","content":"Killing a Primordial wouldn't destroy their concept - but I suspect you're undermining one of their most active and dedicated advocates.<br /> <br /> So slaying SWLIHN doesn't destroy Hierarchy - but man, what would hell look like without all those hierarchy-enforcing-charms keeping the various spirit tiers in check? Plus I recall someplace suggesting that SWLIHN could be a patron or ally to the right Circle (in the circumstances where their goals reinforce Hierarchy). <br /> <br /> Same as killing Autochton won't destroy &quot;invention&quot; or &quot;technology&quot; - but it's still a huge setback. And I can't recall (if it was 1st or 2nd Ed - or perhaps a holdover from World of Darkness Autochtonia) where I saw Autochtonia having some passive technology-related bonuses (machines degrade slower; easier rolls for inventing/crafting; etc).<br /> <hr /><br /> Killing the Sun is an odd one. People often think of Apollo as the &quot;Sun God&quot;, but Apollyon was merely the &quot;Destroyer&quot; - the negative aspects of archery (infection &amp; death). Then you have Helios (the Titan) snuffing him out and the cult of Apollo-Helios claiming he was purified by celestial flame. THEN they flipped and expanded his domains (and upgraded Artemis/Selene/Luna since they're siblings). Or you have Norse myths of moon-and-sun eating wolves.<br /> <br /> Like, part of me thinks &quot;it should be feasible to kill them&quot;.<br /> <br /> And part of me thinks &quot;well, Apollo was never the sun to begin with, he's just an archery-god who got upgraded, so killing him isn't <i>really</i> that much of an achievement&quot;.<br /> <br /> But this is fumbling around mythology - I the only games in which I could imagine wanting to snuff out the sun are those that entail a big green replacement following suit. #HailTheReclamation","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T13:56:51-08:00","id":1283355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1283257-do-the-primordials-embody-their-concepts-or-do-they-just-represent-them?p=1283336#post1283336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Killing a Primordial wouldn't destroy their concept - but I suspect you're undermining one of their most active and dedicated advocates.<br /> <br /> So slaying SWLIHN doesn't destroy Hierarchy - but man, what would hell look like without all those hierarchy-enforcing-charms keeping the various spirit tiers in check? Plus I recall someplace suggesting that SWLIHN could be a patron or ally to the right Circle (in the circumstances where their goals reinforce Hierarchy). <br /> <br /> Same as killing Autochton won't destroy &amp;quot;invention&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;technology&amp;quot; - but it's still a huge setback. And I can't recall (if it was 1st or 2nd Ed - or perhaps a holdover from World of Darkness Autochtonia) where I saw Autochtonia having some passive technology-related bonuses (machines degrade slower; easier rolls for inventing/crafting; etc).<br /> <hr /><br /> Killing the Sun is an odd one. People often think of Apollo as the &amp;quot;Sun God&amp;quot;, but Apollyon was merely the &amp;quot;Destroyer&amp;quot; - the negative aspects of archery (infection &amp; death). Then you have Helios (the Titan) snuffing him out and the cult of Apollo-Helios claiming he was purified by celestial flame. THEN they flipped and expanded his domains (and upgraded Artemis/Selene/Luna since they're siblings). Or you have Norse myths of moon-and-sun eating wolves.<br /> <br /> Like, part of me thinks &amp;quot;it should be feasible to kill them&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> And part of me thinks &amp;quot;well, Apollo was never the sun to begin with, he's just an archery-god who got upgraded, so killing him isn't <i>really</i> that much of an achievement&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> But this is fumbling around mythology - I the only games in which I could imagine wanting to snuff out the sun are those that entail a big green replacement following suit. #HailTheReclamation</div> </div> </div> </div>UCS is Apollo and Hu\u012btzil\u014dp\u014dchtli at minumum. With traits of other gods thrown jn(he keeps Apollo\u2019s mice, but old canon included stories of Yi the archer, he likes human sacrifices, etc). <br /> I don\u2019t think killing the sun has been addressed this edition\u20142e had \u201cif you kill the sun, Ahlat or Little Beam can replace him\u201d in a book but otherwise nothing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T19:07:39-08:00","id":1283410,"title":"","content":"Are the Shinma still a thing in 3e? Because they're the only ones I could really imagine as not existing distinct from the things they define. But...it's honestly difficult to imagine how you would interact with one of them directly, let alone make one stop existing, so I think it's kind of a moot point.<br /> <br /> I mean, Nirguna already defines existence by not existing, so ...how would you even interact with that or make it not not-exist? It's like the empty set, you can't just ....remove that from math or redefine it to be something else, not without making math fall apart, so messing with Nirguna would do something similar, if you even could do that, but I really can't conceive of a way you could do that, not without massive magical BS anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","user":"BrilliantRain","date":". 01-28-2019, 10:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T20:25:31-08:00","id":1283415,"title":"","content":"Also, several Primordials have been killed to give us the Neverbourn, so how would that work?<br /> <br /> &quot;You helped destroy the embodiment of a concept we can no longer remember or think about. Good work heroes. I hope.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> We had enough of that with SWLIHN's hissy fit. (Hurled one of her spheres at Creation and destroyed ninety percent of its reality.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 01-28-2019, 11:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T21:00:58-08:00","id":1283426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1283257-do-the-primordials-embody-their-concepts-or-do-they-just-represent-them?p=1283415#post1283415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, several Primordials have been killed to give us the Neverbourn, so how would that work?<br /> <br /> &quot;You helped destroy the embodiment of a concept we can no longer remember or think about. Good work heroes. I hope.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> We had enough of that with SWLIHN's hissy fit. (Hurled one of her spheres at Creation and destroyed ninety percent of its reality.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Up to 90% of reality. People really had no idea after the fact, but some scholars thought it was as much as 90%. Probably much lower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T21:58:00-08:00","id":1283433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1283257-do-the-primordials-embody-their-concepts-or-do-they-just-represent-them?p=1283410#post1283410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are the Shinma still a thing in 3e? Because they're the only ones I could really imagine as not existing distinct from the things they define. But...it's honestly difficult to imagine how you would interact with one of them directly, let alone make one stop existing, so I think it's kind of a moot point.<br /> <br /> I mean, Nirguna already defines existence by not existing, so ...how would you even interact with that or make it not not-exist? It's like the empty set, you can't just ....remove that from math or redefine it to be something else, not without making math fall apart, so messing with Nirguna would do something similar, if you even could do that, but I really can't conceive of a way you could do that, not without massive magical BS anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the term shinma not even being capitalized originally kind of shows how drift of their perceived importance might ahve been overblown. Kind of rembmer that in the orignal Fair Folk presentation, the shinma weren't for sure even real.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T23:29:47-08:00","id":1283455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1283257-do-the-primordials-embody-their-concepts-or-do-they-just-represent-them?p=1283433#post1283433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the term shinma not even being capitalized originally kind of shows how drift of their perceived importance might ahve been overblown. Kind of rembmer that in the orignal Fair Folk presentation, the shinma weren't for sure even real.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also recall from a perilous answer that I got from the devs in the ask the devs section was that things like shinma and deva were not concepts they ever really had the intention of revisiting, or at least hoping that they wouldn\u2019t, so I think it is being left up to individual tables to decide for themselves. But mostly I came here to post this terry pratchet quote:<br /> <br /> WHAT WOULD HAVE HAPPENED IF YOU HADN'T SAVED HIM?<br /> <br /> &quot;Yes! The sun would have risen just the same, yes?&quot;<br /> <br /> NO<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh, come on. You can't expect me to believe that. It's an astronomical fact.&quot;<br /> <br /> THE SUN WOULD NOT HAVE RISEN.<br /> ...<br /> &quot;Really? Then what would have happened, pray?&quot;<br /> <br /> A MERE BALL OF FLAMING GAS WOULD HAVE ILLUMINATED THE WORLD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <div align=\"left\">Elemental and dragon line descriptors and capturing device coming soon</div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1131843-my-own-take-on-a-craft-rewrite-that-inclu\" target=\"_blank\">Craft Rewrite </a> W/ Points, Slots, and Charms</div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1106793-2nd-circle-demon-c-al-siphar-soc-initiation-symbiosis-of-the-burning-heart-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Demon Adversaries and Related Sorcerous Initiation</a></div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1091536-seeking-thoughts-and-suggestions-on-constructing-an-organization-in-game-specifically-a-university\" target=\"_blank\">Executive Leadership</a> Organization Merrit</div> <hr /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1990-norraba","name":"norraba","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1990_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-29T04:36:07-08:00","id":1283481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1283257-do-the-primordials-embody-their-concepts-or-do-they-just-represent-them?p=1283433#post1283433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the term shinma not even being capitalized originally kind of shows how drift of their perceived importance might ahve been overblown. Kind of rembmer that in the orignal Fair Folk presentation, the shinma weren't for sure even real.</div> </div> </div> </div>More than that was the way they were only mentioned in the introductory blurbs for each of the Graces in the Charms chapter.<br /> <br /> I've always suspected that their inclusion in things like Roll of Glorious Divinities was a matter of a particular writer having become very enamored of their first appearance, and wanting to include them again wherever possible (a foundation that other writers picked up on for various things in and out of books).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-29T09:57:37-08:00","id":1283528,"title":"","content":"They are probably fine as members of the group of things that includes the Saigoth gate. They probably don't exist, but a group of people you might interact with has some philosophical/religious attachment to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-29T10:31:21-08:00","id":1283534,"title":"","content":"Killing SWLiHN would not destroy hierarchy, no. However, the Yozis are very much bound by their nature, to a far greater degree than those who came after them.<br /> <br /> That is, I highly doubt that SWLiHN could do something truly anti-authoritarian.<br /> <br /> In terms of what happens if a god (or other celestial being that has control over a portfolio) dies, I imagine that it would explain how things change over time. To use a real-life example, the very nature of war as an element of state influence changed after WWI. (It was changing slowly over time, but WWI definitely nailed that coffin.) Before WWI, the idea of going to war to gain a positive (and generally limited) goal was widely accepted. After it, only 'evil' states (such as were present in the Axis powers of WWII) held this view, with all others restricted themselves to the idea of war as a defensive tool only... (at least on paper... don't want to get into proxy wars)<br /> <br /> Anyway, one way to explain this shift in a world with a literal Celestial bureaucracy is that the old god of war retired/died/whatever, and a new god of war, with a different view on war, ascended. (Another is that the god who held the portfolio of war's view shifted, but that is less... dramatic.) This can also explain how to change Yozis over time, if the Soul Menagerie concept of them still holds in 3E.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3551-ulthwithian","name":"Ulthwithian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-29T12:28:45-08:00","id":1283555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1283257-do-the-primordials-embody-their-concepts-or-do-they-just-represent-them?p=1283355#post1283355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> UCS is Apollo and Hu\u012btzil\u014dp\u014dchtli at minumum. With traits of other gods thrown jn(he keeps Apollo\u2019s mice, but old canon included stories of Yi the archer, he likes human sacrifices, etc). <br /> I don\u2019t think killing the sun has been addressed this edition\u20142e had \u201cif you kill the sun, Ahlat or Little Beam can replace him\u201d in a book but otherwise nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually there are two details that went into more note than that. Return of the Empress revealed that if UcS died, the sun would be kept aflame by the Greater Elemental Dragon of Fire bound inside it as a pilot light. The result of this is that it would turn from gold to red, and lose all negative effects on creatures with magic vulnerabilities to sunlight, and the Holy Keyword would cease to function (unless a Solar has an Integrity Charm to back it up themselves instead of invoking the UcS\u2019s Creature of Darkness list).<br /> <br /> Glories of the Maidens (written after RotE but released first) has an Astrology Charm that allows a Sidereal to bestow a willing subject with the destiny and rank of a deceased deity. This is the intended mechanism by which the UcS could be replaced.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s all 2E of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-29T15:25:15-08:00","id":1283575,"title":"","content":"We're in a situation in our Sidereals game where The Unconquered Sun is dead (or at least it seems that way) and the main thing we want him for is to take his turns in the Games of Divinity because with Luna or one of the Maidens leading the games constantly it's plunged Yu-Shan into darkness that's really not helped the behaviour in its inhabitants and the plants up there still grow via sunlight. There's magical solutions to this, but it's going to massively drive up the price of food for the people there who actually need to eat.<br /> <br /> I find the whole thing darkly amusing, because we're basically looking for a puppet to shake hands, cut ceremonial ribbons and not shake things up too much. To that end we'd look so much like typical Sidereal bad guys who want to control everything to a group of Solar Exalted hoping for a proactive Unconquered Sun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-29T15:57:22-08:00","id":1283587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1283257-do-the-primordials-embody-their-concepts-or-do-they-just-represent-them?p=1283575#post1283575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're in a situation in our Sidereals game where The Unconquered Sun is dead (or at least it seems that way) and the main thing we want him for is to take his turns in the Games of Divinity because with Luna or one of the Maidens leading the games constantly it's plunged Yu-Shan into darkness that's really not helped the behaviour in its inhabitants and the plants up there still grow via sunlight. There's magical solutions to this, but it's going to massively drive up the price of food for the people there who actually need to eat.<br /> <br /> I find the whole thing darkly amusing, because we're basically looking for a puppet to shake hands, cut ceremonial ribbons and not shake things up too much. To that end we'd look so much like typical Sidereal bad guys who want to control everything to a group of Solar Exalted hoping for a proactive Unconquered Sun.</div> </div> </div> </div>not all of the pcs agree with the idea of just finding an easy to use puppet though","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-29T16:49:21-08:00","id":1283593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1283257-do-the-primordials-embody-their-concepts-or-do-they-just-represent-them?p=1283587#post1283587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> not all of the pcs agree with the idea of just finding an easy to use puppet though</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you considered an easily directed pawn then? Or you can go and plagiarize the Realm and find someone just competent enough to not make everything worse, but not competent enough to be able to anything with their authority. Probably best not to use Regent Fokuf though, he's probably paranoid enough about the Great Houses deciding to kill him if he becomes a problem without a more active heresy under his belt and knowing he has the attention of people who have so many better ways to end him than most DBs do. :3","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-29T21:49:51-08:00","id":1283655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1283257-do-the-primordials-embody-their-concepts-or-do-they-just-represent-them?p=1283269#post1283269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually I think in 3E one of the defining qualities of the Incarnae is supposed to be that they break this rule. The Unconquered Sun really is the sun, and if he died it may well go out.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Incarnae are slightly more connected to the things they manage than most other things in the setting, but even then, it's meant to be a &quot;specific&quot; sort of connection arising from their circumstances rather than a transcendent platonic form sort of thing. That is to say, at least in 2e, it was implied that the sun would be affected (though it wouldn't snuff out) if the UCS died, but that's because the sun itself is a physical thing directly tied to him and not because the UCS is some sole platonic embodiment of the concept of &quot;sun&quot; (or &quot;perfection&quot; or anything else.)<br /> <br /> Similarly, if you killed the Maidens, Fate itself wouldn't immediately grind to a halt or anything like that - there was a time when they were manually running the Loom, but that's long gone. But the Sidereals would have to probably do even more work to compensate for some things that the Maidens were accomplishing by their simple presence or occasional attention, and might have to seek out substitutes in some form in order to keep Fate running smoothly in the long term.<br /> <br /> The Primordials <i>once</i> probably had similar connections to various parts of Creation, but even before the war those were being offloaded to the Incarnae (that was the point of the Incarnae), and those that were left were largely severed long ago, with their roles either replaced or whatever damage their loss entailed already being fully-felt. There are likely a few exceptions - killing SWLIHN shouldn't be <i>completely</i> without consequence. Viewing Creation as a program again, I wouldn't be surprised if there's still a few object references to her still tucked away in hidden corners of the setting where the Exalted failed to root them out (although she herself probably ripped most of those out in the Three Spheres Cataclysm.) But it wouldn't cause hierarchy itself to collapse or anything of that nature - more like occasional weirdness for a while similar to fate errors, or the odd thing sealed deep in Creation getting released, or plot-hooks like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 01-30-2019, 12:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-29T22:01:35-08:00","id":1283656,"title":"","content":"I seem to recall some of the descriptions of Zen-Mu had the Primordials, or at least their world bodies, forming a more significant part of the world. They appear to have moved away from that setup with Creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-30T02:47:18-08:00","id":1283672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1283257-do-the-primordials-embody-their-concepts-or-do-they-just-represent-them?p=1283415#post1283415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, several Primordials have been killed to give us the Neverbourn, so how would that work?<br /> <br /> &quot;You helped destroy the embodiment of a concept we can no longer remember or think about. Good work heroes. I hope.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> We had enough of that with SWLIHN's hissy fit. (Hurled one of her spheres at Creation and destroyed ninety percent of its reality.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> i think one book explicitly says that &quot; the neverborn took a lot of things with them in their grave&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-30T11:54:04-08:00","id":1283758,"title":"","content":"It should be noted that SHLiHN taking-out 90% of everythign in her thing was only stated in <b>Dreams of the First Age</b>. Depending on where you place that in canon (1e was very vague on the number, and 3e runs with a lot of stuff with the Yozis at least being based on <b>Games of Divinity</b> and that's it) affects a bit on this. I honestly kind of doubt it might come back as it leads to weird over-thinking onw aht was I think meant to be a bit of weird, not some definitive &quot;The world is fucked&quot; thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-31T10:12:17-08:00","id":1283959,"title":"","content":"Correction: I conflated Cecelyne with SWLIHN. But onwards!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1283257-do-the-primordials-embody-their-concepts-or-do-they-just-represent-them?p=1283655#post1283655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Primordials <i>once</i> probably had similar connections to various parts of Creation, but even before the war those were being offloaded to the Incarnae (that was the point of the Incarnae), and those that were left were largely severed long ago, with their roles either replaced or whatever damage their loss entailed already being fully-felt. There are likely a few exceptions - killing SWLIHN shouldn't be <i>completely</i> without consequence. Viewing Creation as a program again, I wouldn't be surprised if there's still a few object references to her still tucked away in hidden corners of the setting where the Exalted failed to root them out (although she herself probably ripped most of those out in the Three Spheres Cataclysm.) But it wouldn't cause hierarchy itself to collapse or anything of that nature - more like occasional weirdness for a while similar to fate errors, or the odd thing sealed deep in Creation getting released, or plot-hooks like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>Deliberately Deleting Good Mechanics</b></span><br /> <br /> One of the things I admire about Exalted are the mechanics - being able to articulate previously nebulous ideas (from other RPGs) into firmer rules (especially social/mental/virtues). Clear mechanics eliminate doubt and ensure folks feel they actually earned their success (by luck or skill) and that the ST isn't just going easy/hard on them arbitrarily.<br /> <br /> The first way I could imagine &quot;things falling apart&quot; is when &quot;hard-coded&quot; rules now become vague guidelines - let's go backwards!<br /> <br /> Cecelyne's charms often hard-code social hierarchies into charms via UMI - but imagine forever-deleting those charms and being a god or Exalted scholar trying to remember them?<ul><li>Social charms suddenly can hit anyone - low-Essence spirits can hit high-Essence spirits just as effectively.</li> <li>Hierarchy charms suddenly fail altogether - the comparison between relative Essence is no longer sustained and thus charms predicated on that come up with a #null when trying to get an integer for calculation.</li> </ul>Or kill Malfeas - and the closest thing you get to his charms is self-shaping (Lunar style) or earth-aspected emulations. <br /> <br /> Or kill Luna - and the closest thing you get to shapeshifting is D&amp;D Druids (abandoning all the awesome heartsblood stuff and warform and the like). No more Gifts, no more Warform. The remnants of her champions being Beastmen. Or if you like Werewolf crossover, breed them with Totemic gods (so God-Blooded Beastmen tribes).<br /> <br /> Every time you kill off some Primordial-tier creature, mechanics crumble....so in-character, <i><b>intellectually</b></i> it seems nothing changed (concepts haven't been deleted) but it <i><b>feels</b></i> like things aren't working like they once did (because results are no longer reliable or the same).<br /> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>Tangent: History Falls Apart</b></span><br /> <br /> This makes me think of how much of mythology, folk legend and even paintings - where people of the period think their references are universal - and then they fall apart centuries later.<br /> <br /> <b>Example: Atlas &amp; the Sky</b><ul><li>Modern depictions often erroneously depict Atlas holding up the globe...</li> <li>BUT he's supposed to hold up a celestial sphere (Uranus).</li> <li>Modern minds would object &quot;but it's impossible to hold up the sky/space!&quot;</li> <li>BUT many classical cultures thought the sky was solid.</li> <li>Modern minds would object &quot;if the sky was solid, it'd fall and crush us! or it'd block the sun!&quot;</li> <li>BUT there were even some Middle-Eastern cultures who believe the sky was a dome of metal (and the stars were gods living on it, looking down at us); or look at Taoism associating metal with air.</li> <li>Modern minds would object &quot;but metal belongs with earth &amp; minerals - not air!&quot;</li> <li>BUT people observed that when metal gets cold, moisture condenses on it - ergo &quot;water comes from metal&quot;. And metal reflects light. So the sky must be a giant metal dome - when the sun comes out (like a torch), the dome lights up - and when it gets too cold, you get rain. Science!</li> </ul>You get a flying Saint like Saint Joseph of Cupertino? Historians misremember it as &quot;madness from ergot-infected grain&quot; or &quot;an extremely agile and gymnastic idiot-savant&quot;. <br /> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>Three Spheres Cataclysm</b></span><br /> <br /> From all of this....the TSC as a cascade failure when the Exalted slew the Neverborn and/or crippled the Yozis.<br /> <br /> They blame it on SWLHN and Hierarchy - but it's not her fault that the Exalted destroyed the foundations and then freaked out when the house crumbles in.<br /> <br /> It's like blaming Malfeas &amp; Cecelyne for the corruption of the Celestial Bureaucracy - their charms could quickly enforce order - it's not their fault they're imprisoned. (But of course, no one would lodge this complaint, since admitting Heaven is corrupt would be politically incorrect).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-31T12:06:50-08:00","id":1283977,"title":"","content":"Again, editions matter in this. 2e took very hard to the &quot;Rules are physics&quot; thing, but 1e didn't and 3e explicitly rejects this. Mostly since while &quot;rules as physics' Is a good experiment, it's not actually (I think) a good way to make a broadly usable game setting. It becomes self-serving solipsistic writing rather htan useful for like, playing hte game.<br /> <br /> My own view is kind of hinted at above. If you kill She Who Lives in Her Name, you don't suddenly change Hierarchy. You just canned its greatest advocate. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar169_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"169\" data-vbnamecard=\"169\">wastevens</a> I think had the best take on it. Hierarchy isn't like, a real <i>thing</i>. At least, it's not something that you can go out and say &quot;That's Hierarchy&quot; in the world like you do an object. At least, anymore in Creation than you can in our universe. It's a relationship, that has some criteria and values to it. The being who probably first emphasized it, recognized it and wanted Creation to engender it, and so on. But it's not like, a thing floating somewhere in a box that didn't exist before SHLiHN and will not work anymore if she's not. It's just that it wasn't able to be expressed until she was around (maybe) and she happens to like it when it emerged in her contributions of Creation.<br /> <br /> A world where there is all these programing analogs that could be analyzed is interesting as a thought experiment, but it ultimately is getting kind of in weeds that don't matter for a lot of games. And I think even starts getting contradictory to a lot of how the game is presented. The Games of Divinity for instance are explicilty nothing to do with mortals. The Incarna are weird in relations to their purviews, but note that the things they are specifically gods of (their various planets) are objects that have symbology. Virtue, light, and whatnot would exist if the Sun weren't there. I would go so far as to say that in 3e, if the Unconquered Sun were to die, the actual like, planet that is the sun would just keep moving, although maybe go off kilter as it requires insane checking and maintenance that the god provided. There's a lot of ways to describe the ways the Incarna are related to their purviews, without having them be some special case where aspects of Creation immediatley break or stop making sense for humans from Earth if they were no longer there, I feel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-01T07:03:20-08:00","id":1284124,"title":"","content":"I'd contend that for practical purposes there's no metaphysical constant, but that it depends on whether you can imagine a world without it. Destroying the Unconquered Sun and living in a moonlit world is interesting, destroying him and living in a world without the concept of excellence and enlightenment is less so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-02T01:42:04-08:00","id":1284303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The first way I could imagine &quot;things falling apart&quot; is when &quot;hard-coded&quot; rules now become vague guidelines - let's go backwards! </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1283257-do-the-primordials-embody-their-concepts-or-do-they-just-represent-them?p=1283977#post1283977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, editions matter in this. 2e took very hard to the &quot;Rules are physics&quot; thing, but 1e didn't and 3e explicitly rejects this. Mostly since while &quot;rules as physics' Is a good experiment, it's not actually (I think) a good way to make a broadly usable game setting. It becomes self-serving solipsistic writing rather htan useful for like, playing hte game.<br /> <br /> My own view is kind of hinted at above. If you kill She Who Lives in Her Name, you don't suddenly change Hierarchy. You just canned its greatest advocate. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar169_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"169\" data-vbnamecard=\"169\">wastevens</a> I think had the best take on it. Hierarchy isn't like, a real <i>thing</i>. At least, it's not something that you can go out and say &quot;That's Hierarchy&quot; in the world like you do an object. At least, anymore in Creation than you can in our universe. It's a relationship, that has some criteria and values to it. The being who probably first emphasized it, recognized it and wanted Creation to engender it, and so on. But it's not like, a thing floating somewhere in a box that didn't exist before SHLiHN and will not work anymore if she's not. It's just that it wasn't able to be expressed until she was around (maybe) and she happens to like it when it emerged in her contributions of Creation.<br /> <br /> A world where there is all these programing analogs that could be analyzed is interesting as a thought experiment, but it ultimately is getting kind of in weeds that don't matter for a lot of games. And I think even starts getting contradictory to a lot of how the game is presented. The Games of Divinity for instance are explicilty nothing to do with mortals. The Incarna are weird in relations to their purviews, but note that the things they are specifically gods of (their various planets) are objects that have symbology. Virtue, light, and whatnot would exist if the Sun weren't there. I would go so far as to say that in 3e, if the Unconquered Sun were to die, the actual like, planet that is the sun would just keep moving, although maybe go off kilter as it requires insane checking and maintenance that the god provided. There's a lot of ways to describe the ways the Incarna are related to their purviews, without having them be some special case where aspects of Creation immediatley break or stop making sense for humans from Earth if they were no longer there, I feel.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the second post gets at an important point. (Which, in retrospect, I should have emphasized in my post a bit more, but I just sort of took it for granted that people would see it.) We're talking Watsonian reasons, but we need to step back and look at the Doylist ones for a moment.<br /> <br /> Having the entire universe collapse when SWLIHN dies (or drastically alter itself to the extent of an entire defining aspect of reality snapping out of existence) isn't very fun. It might sound fun to some people, but in practice it isn't playable in most games, which means that if someone says &quot;killing SWLIHN destroys hierarchy&quot; what they're really saying is &quot;you can't actually allow your players to kill SWLIHN ever.&quot; I suspect there's some people who find that statement cool, but that leads into the second reason why killing her can't be <i>that</i> seismic of an event.<br /> <br /> Because there's also story / thematic constraints to consider. In Exalted, as a story or a setting? SWLIHN is not <i>that</i> important. She's a side-character. Yes, she's a really big powerful side-character, but the game is not about her, and while you could make her the focus (in the same way you could make any character the focus), she's not the focus by default. Making her death seismic on a level that drastically alters the setting is bad because it sends the message that SWLIHN is more important than she is; and, by extension, it diminishes the weight and value of the rest of the setting. It means that all the kings and kingdoms of Creation don't matter as much, because if someone could just go beat SWLIHN to death the rug would be yanked out from under all of them. That's not a message the game should send.<br /> <br /> <i>That said</i>. The whole point of the Yozis is to be ridiculously, stupidly big and scary so Infernals and Sorcerers can look cool by stealing their stuff and so, sometimes, in certain kinds of games, you can punch their faces in anyway. And in service of that goal, it's fair to say that punching SWLIHN's face in should do <i>something</i>. There's room to have her death cause Creation-wide ripples without having it just yank the rug out from under everyone as if she's the only thing that mattered.<br /> <br /> So what should those ripples be? Some of this ought to vary based on the nature of your game and the expectations of your players, but I would argue that:<br /> <br /> 1. You want to avoid the idea of broad, open-ended changes to reality, because that breaks &quot;the game is not about SWLiHN&quot; constraint. Maybe for specific games that would be fine, but if I was writing a general rule... no. Nothing about Creation being irrevocably lessened or the true majesty of what was lost being impossible to measure or anything like that. Maybe that was fine in the backstory, but this has to exist in a world where the <i>core</i> focus is on game-of-thrones, queens-and-castles play. SWLiHN's death might cause disasters, but it should be stuff that can be addressed on that level of play, not cosmic transcendent metaphysical disasters that render the knights-and-castles meaningless.<br /> <br /> 2. You want it to be stuff that leads to interesting gameplay going forwards - in other words, story hooks. Look at the stuff I suggested. &quot;The Maidens died, so now the Sidereals have to find someone or something to replace the role they played for the Loom&quot; is a story hook. &quot;SWLiHN died, so now the seals on the ancient Behemoth of Anarchy that she sealed in the time before time have begun to weaken and crack&quot; is a story hook. &quot;The UCS died, so you must go on a quest to recover the First Flame so that it can be used to rekindle the dying sun&quot; is a story hook.<br /> <br /> &quot;SWLiHN died, so now everything is worse forever in some vague undefinable way&quot; or &quot;Malfeas died, so now we're going to arbitrarily change the rules of the setting&quot; isn't a story hook. It doesn't improve anything. It's just wanking an NPC. In some situations, yeah, maybe your players want it to <i>really</i> drive home what a big deal it is that they killed SWLiHN, but it certainly wouldn't be my default assumption.<br /> <br /> (I think it is absolutely worthwhile to come up with technobabble / magical-metaphysics reasons to justify the stuff I mentioned as a good outcome - that was a lot of what my post was going for. If a game is at the point where your players are actually punching SWLiHN in the face, I think they'd probably want to hear some sort of meaningful-sounding statement about how grand and significant their actions were. I just assumed that people would realize that in <i>actually</i> all of that is just written in reverse in order to reach a predetermined conclusion, which is determined by what makes a good game.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-02T05:07:19-08:00","id":1284322,"title":"","content":"For She Who Lives in Her Name specifically, I think there would be something interesting in following that line from her original write-up about her willingness to offer advice and aid, with the notion that a surprising amount starts falling apart with her death (either in literal metaphysical terms or organisational ones), revealing that a lot of Heaven and Earth had been more compromised by her than anybody had suspected.<br /> <br /> I'd say the more important consequence of that than the immediate breakdowns would be the reveal of how many authorities in Creation didn't know what they were doing, and were willing to accept or solicit Her aid to make up for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-03T08:45:32-08:00","id":1284506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1283257-do-the-primordials-embody-their-concepts-or-do-they-just-represent-them?p=1283977#post1283977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, editions matter in this. 2e took very hard to the &quot;Rules are physics&quot; thing, but 1e didn't and 3e explicitly rejects this. Mostly since while &quot;rules as physics' Is a good experiment, it's not actually (I think) a good way to make a broadly usable game setting. It becomes self-serving solipsistic writing rather htan useful for like, playing hte game.<br /> <br /> My own view is kind of hinted at above. If you kill She Who Lives in Her Name, you don't suddenly change Hierarchy. You just canned its greatest advocate. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar169_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"169\" data-vbnamecard=\"169\">wastevens</a> I think had the best take on it. Hierarchy isn't like, a real <i>thing</i>. At least, it's not something that you can go out and say &quot;That's Hierarchy&quot; in the world like you do an object. At least, anymore in Creation than you can in our universe. It's a relationship, that has some criteria and values to it. The being who probably first emphasized it, recognized it and wanted Creation to engender it, and so on. But it's not like, a thing floating somewhere in a box that didn't exist before SHLiHN and will not work anymore if she's not. It's just that it wasn't able to be expressed until she was around (maybe) and she happens to like it when it emerged in her contributions of Creation.<br /> <br /> A world where there is all these programing analogs that could be analyzed is interesting as a thought experiment, but it ultimately is getting kind of in weeds that don't matter for a lot of games. And I think even starts getting contradictory to a lot of how the game is presented. The Games of Divinity for instance are explicilty nothing to do with mortals. The Incarna are weird in relations to their purviews, but note that the things they are specifically gods of (their various planets) are objects that have symbology. Virtue, light, and whatnot would exist if the Sun weren't there. I would go so far as to say that in 3e, if the Unconquered Sun were to die, the actual like, planet that is the sun would just keep moving, although maybe go off kilter as it requires insane checking and maintenance that the god provided. There's a lot of ways to describe the ways the Incarna are related to their purviews, without having them be some special case where aspects of Creation immediatley break or stop making sense for humans from Earth if they were no longer there, I feel.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> by that logic though it doesn't make much sense that the exalted imprisoned the yozis instead of killing them. I remember one book saying that primordial death had consequences the exalted had learned to fear. Also apparently Salina had a vision of how the universe would be if SWLIHN died.. and she rather liked it<br /> <br /> and what about the shinma? beings similar to the primordials except for the fact that they are the opposite of what they embody. One book explicity said&quot; before the shinma of separation awoke or things were united(or whatever his title is)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-03T09:09:32-08:00","id":1284513,"title":"","content":"A) That was second edition, which leaned WAY harder into ' Primordials are foundational to concepts'. Even then, it varied from writer to writer.<br /> <br /> B) Even then, the foremost reason given for the Exalted not murdering all the Primordials was because Gaia pled for mercy for her siblings.<br /> <br /> C) The creation of the Underworld is plenty freaky enough as an additive consequence to not need subtractive consequences.<br /> <br /> D) The shinma is 1e we're introduced more as conceptual/philosophical/allegorical concepts, which the base seized on personifying because fans. Which then became ascended fanon in 2e's elaboration on the metaphysics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-03T09:39:02-08:00","id":1284521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1283257-do-the-primordials-embody-their-concepts-or-do-they-just-represent-them?p=1284506#post1284506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> by that logic though it doesn't make much sense that the exalted imprisoned the yozis instead of killing them.</div> </div> </div> </div>By the logic of &quot;everything breaks if we kill the Yozis&quot;, the gods and Exalted can't be fully ready to execute them before Gaia advocates for clemency. Even Second Edition had that line.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember one book saying that primordial death had consequences the exalted had learned to fear.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, shadowlands.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">and what about the shinma? beings</div> </div> </div> </div>The shinma aren't really beings. More weird abstractions of reality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">One book explicity said&amp;quot; before the shinma of separation awoke or things were united(or whatever his title is)</div> </div> </div> </div>That was a book that read that Advaita Iruivan was God and assumed that meant it was important, overlooking how it was an aspect of Nirguna, which does not exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-03T09:56:02-08:00","id":1284524,"title":"","content":"&quot;The concepts that underpin Creation are independent of the Shinma. That was the whole point. Shima can be turned on and off on a whim. They're pale imitations of reality the fair folk used to play their games.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-03T10:36:05-08:00","id":1284542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1283257-do-the-primordials-embody-their-concepts-or-do-they-just-represent-them?p=1284506#post1284506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> by that logic though it doesn't make much sense that the exalted imprisoned the yozis instead of killing them. I remember one book saying that primordial death had consequences that Exalted had learned to fear</div> </div> </div> </div>When the Exalted killed their first Primordial, it created a rip in reality through to a dimension of darkness. With each Primordial slain, there were more uncloseable holes, and that dark dimension filled with the twisted souls of devas. <br /> And then it began to fill with spirits that looked like dead humans... And the Exalted realised they'd broken reincarnation itself, damning some humans to be trapped in the nightmares of dead Primordials.<br /> At that point, they decided to avoid killing more Primordials.<br /> <br /> I'm not massively bothered by Primordials being linked to concepts, but it's not necessary to explain why the Exalted imprisoned them instead of killing them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-03T14:23:05-08:00","id":1284571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1283257-do-the-primordials-embody-their-concepts-or-do-they-just-represent-them?p=1284506#post1284506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">by that logic though it doesn't make much sense that the exalted imprisoned the yozis instead of killing them. I remember one book saying that primordial death had consequences the exalted had learned to fear. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>As already noted by others, the creation or at least, linking to the Underworld that the death of the god's enemies caused was probably something they didn't want to add to. Killing a titan need not delete concepts to be destructive. They can just...be destructive, without having a setting suddenly be unrecognizable to humans playing the game.<br /> <br /> There is also the couple-times-referred-to clemency pleas from Gaia, the possibility that killing the ones who were left wasn't any easier than locking up those who surrendered, some enterprising Exalt proposing enslavement of the to-be-Yozis, and so on. There's plenty of reasons to not kill them besides some brain-spidery navel-gazing about a setting that need not have it or is bettered by it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1283257-do-the-primordials-embody-their-concepts-or-do-they-just-represent-them?p=1284506#post1284506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Also apparently Salina had a vision of how the universe would be if SWLIHN died.. and she rather liked it</div> </div> </div> </div>Of any book to have the &quot;Depends on edition&quot; skepticism to it, <b>Dreams of the First Age</b> is up there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1283257-do-the-primordials-embody-their-concepts-or-do-they-just-represent-them?p=1284506#post1284506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and what about the shinma? beings similar to the primordials except for the fact that they are the opposite of what they embody. One book explicity said&quot; before the shinma of separation awoke or things were united(or whatever his title is)</div> </div> </div> </div>Whether the shinma were even real was something that shifted from their original discussion in <b>Exalted: the Fair Folk</b> (where it was not clear they were anything but raksha attempts to describe things we living in a universe of those things take for granted), plus as noted ascended fanon on how they were. And the thing on Advaita Iraivan further hurts this as<i> it was not supposed to be important</i> in the original presentation. There's a reason that the current devs have noted that the shinma might not even be mentioend as the issues they bring aren't worth the wordcount.<br /> <br /> Dharma is the princible of entropy and change. And the absence of that might be Dharma. But whether Dharma is real or the raksha talking about osme mythical thing state that doesn't exist in the universe currently or potentially never has historiclaly, is something originally very vague. And was that until they suddenly were reified in <b>Roll of Glorious Divinity I</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-03T14:41:01-08:00","id":1284580,"title":"","content":"My position is that the destruction of things wrought by the murder of the Primordials is probably the same reason various stuff blew up during the Usurpation - namely, the creators of the works may well have created inadvertent (or advertent) dead-man's switches into said works. It's not so much that <i>the notion of a thing's existence</i> hinges on the continued existence of a given titan, so much as that Gaia (for example) might have put a little more work into Creation's geomancy than her killers are necessarily aware of. Her death wouldn't cause the five elements to stop existing, but some prominent manses around Creation may blow up because no one knows to regulate the flow of Essence along that dragon-line anymore.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-03T19:45:22-08:00","id":1284636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1283257-do-the-primordials-embody-their-concepts-or-do-they-just-represent-them?p=1284571#post1284571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whether the shinma were even real was something that shifted from their original discussion in <b>Exalted: the Fair Folk</b> (where it was not clear they were anything but raksha attempts to describe things we living in a universe of those things take for granted)</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, people with a strictly materialistic worldview might take them for granted. Historically, people have often not taken reality for granted and devised all kinds of theological, metaphysical and philosophical premises underlying and originating it.<br /> <br /> Heck, even within materialism, some would argue that things like string theory constitute an inability to take basic principles of physics for granted, that there needs to be an essential underlying function to explain why things work the way that they do. Plus that whole conundrum of resolving the temporal finiteness of the universe, and speculating on the subject of how it began, what it means for there to have been a before its beginning, and why the way it currently looks doesn't make sense.<br /> <br /> As to the shinma, I do accept that part of it is that fantasy fiction in general has a problem with the premise that not everything people believe in needs to be true, or self-evident. I think the First Edition writing understood a lot of that in an understated way, Second Edition often opted to utilise or fill in such things in ways that made them real or evident or accounted for in the simple cosmology, and Third Edition is showing good signs of expressing it more overtly with things like a detailed monotheistic religion that isn't written as somebody's deceptive scheme.<br /> <br /> With the shinma and the Raksha, I think it ought to be some combination of them having a belief system, and making a show of having deeper cosmological knowledge than the Creation-born (which they're probably lying or deluded about, but maybe not).<br /> <br /> For the Yozis, considering that a lot of cases won't involve killing them, I think that compelling drama can come from them making convincing (if hard to completely follow) arguments to the effect that doing so will cause fundamental damage to Creation, or reality as a whole. Not even as a bluff to call or a thing to create hesitation around something they might or could do; I think scenes of such strange interactions can be rewarding in their own right, and possibly some resulting Intimacies might shape character/player behaviour in novel and unexpected ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-03T22:27:10-08:00","id":1284663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1283257-do-the-primordials-embody-their-concepts-or-do-they-just-represent-them?p=1284571#post1284571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of any book to have the &quot;Depends on edition&quot; skepticism to it, <b>Dreams of the First Age</b> is up there.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, DotFA is situated at a weird ideological turning point in the portrayal of Primordials and kind of a fucking mess because of it.<br /> <br /> It was when the portrayal of the Primordial War started shifting to a relatively short conflict that the Exalted won because they were battle ready and their opponents weren't, relatively short and a lot of Celestials seemed to approach it like Legolas and Gimili in the Lord of the Rings movies trying to wrack up the most kills (with likely a good portion of the casualties happening because people were more worried about their score). But you can see bits of the older fan perception of self-guided Exaltations and sheer attrition being the secret to victory against vastly superior opponents who could rewrite reality on a whim shine through in places.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T04:47:23-08:00","id":1285205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1283257-do-the-primordials-embody-their-concepts-or-do-they-just-represent-them?p=1284513#post1284513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A) That was second edition, which leaned WAY harder into ' Primordials are foundational to concepts'. Even then, it varied from writer to writer.<br /> <br /> B) Even then, the foremost reason given for the Exalted not murdering all the Primordials was because Gaia pled for mercy for her siblings.<br /> <br /> C) The creation of the Underworld is plenty freaky enough as an additive consequence to not need subtractive consequences.<br /> <br /> D) The shinma is 1e we're introduced more as conceptual/philosophical/allegorical concepts, which the base seized on personifying because fans. Which then became ascended fanon in 2e's elaboration on the metaphysics.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest the idea that the exalted showed mercy because it was asked of them.. is totally at odds with how they have behaved through history.. plus the primordials were not even similar beings with whom they could empathise<br /> <br /> Damn, the third edition is still so new(with 2 or three books out?) that i completely forget about it. i'm not sure if it even makes sense to say&quot; this was a second edition thing&quot;<br /> <br /> i always forget to write this distinction in the original posts...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","user":"mark","date":". 02-06-2019, 07:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T14:01:09-08:00","id":1285680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1283257-do-the-primordials-embody-their-concepts-or-do-they-just-represent-them?p=1285205#post1285205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be honest the idea that the exalted showed mercy because it was asked of them.. is totally at odds with how they have behaved through history.. plus the primordials were not even similar beings with whom they could empathise</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Temperance and Compassion were Virtues as well as Valor and Conviction.<br /> The Exalted Host has been portrayed as more crazed and more bloodthirsty over time, in part, to subvert the idea of 'shiny happy people in a perfect utopia', but they are human- where the falling angel meets the rising ape. Sometimes, they will smash a country so totally as to erase it from history, or build a mountain of skulls, or dump all the writings of a great library into a river such that the waters run black from the ink. And sometimes, they can show mercy, even to mortal enemies, even beings they cannot fathom save to know that they would not show mercy given the same chance. It's not rational. But it is deeply human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T16:55:53-08:00","id":1285730,"title":"","content":"Beyond what we are, as a species and people, I think that touches on what we'd wish that we were.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"